milestones.description:
Given m\in[-\sqrt3,\sqrt3], check which of the principal minor conditions from the matrix
A=\begin{pmatrix}1&1&m\\1&2&n\\m&n&3\end{pmatrix}
are already automatically satisfied, and identify the only nontrivial conditions that remain on n.

Check two boundary cases of the candidate interval
m-\sqrt{3-m^2}\le n\le m+\sqrt{3-m^2}
for m\in[-\sqrt3,\sqrt3]:
(1) when m=0, what interval for n is obtained?
(2) when m=\pm\sqrt3, what interval for n is obtained?
These should be consistent with the determinant condition \det A=(3-m^2)-(n-m)^2\ge0.
